<path d="M9.66897 9.67087L14 14.0019M14 14.0019L18.331 18.3329M14 14.0019L18.331 9.67087M14 14.0019L9.66897 18.3329" stroke="#D1D1D1" stroke-width="1.90989" stroke-linecap="round"/>
</svg></div></div><div class="accordion-item-content"><div class="accordion-item-content-details"><div class="text-size-medium text-color-gery">Brokerages can integrate once with zerohash to offer buying, selling, custody, and settlement without building or operating trading infrastructure internally.</div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="faq_item w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion-wrapper"></div><div class="accordion-item"><div class="accordion-item-title"><div class="heading-style-h5 faq_q"> What does zerohash handle versus the brokerage?</div><div class="accordion-item-icon w-embed"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
<path d="M9.66897 9.67087L14 14.0019M14 14.0019L18.331 18.3329M14 14.0019L18.331 9.67087M14 14.0019L9.66897 18.3329" stroke="#D1D1D1" stroke-width="1.90989" stroke-linecap="round"/>
</svg></div></div><div class="accordion-item-content"><div class="accordion-item-content-details"><div class="text-size-medium text-color-gery">zerohash manages execution, custody, asset movement, and compliance infrastructure. The brokerage controls the user experience, pricing, and product strategy.</div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="faq_item w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion-wrapper"></div><div class="accordion-item"><div class="accordion-item-title"><div class="heading-style-h5 faq_q"> How do brokerages manage custody and compliance?</div><div class="accordion-item-icon w-embed"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
<path d="M9.66897 9.67087L14 14.0019M14 14.0019L18.331 18.3329M14 14.0019L18.331 9.67087M14 14.0019L9.66897 18.3329" stroke="#D1D1D1" stroke-width="1.90989" stroke-linecap="round"/>
</svg></div></div><div class="accordion-item-content"><div class="accordion-item-content-details"><div class="text-size-medium text-color-gery">zerohash provides qualified custody and applies consistent compliance controls across all trading activity, reducing operational burden for brokerage teams.</div></div></div></div></div><div role="listitem" class="faq_item w-dyn-item"><div class="accordion-wrapper"></div><div class="accordion-item"><div class="accordion-item-title"><div class="heading-style-h5 faq_q"> Is this built for high-volume platforms?</div><div class="accordion-item-icon w-embed"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
<path d="M9.66897 9.67087L14 14.0019M14 14.0019L18.331 18.3329M14 14.0019L18.331 9.67087M14 14.0019L9.66897 18.3329" stroke="#D1D1D1" stroke-width="1.90989" stroke-linecap="round"/>
</svg></div></div><div class="accordion-item-content"><div class="accordion-item-content-details"><div class="text-size-medium text-color-gery">Yes. zerohash is designed for uptime, reliability, and scale across large brokerage and trading environments.</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="w-embed w-script"><style id="zh-faq-v6">
